            <ArticleTitle>Reflecting Before Testing : Comment on &quot;Personal Genomic Testing, Genetic Inheritance, and Uncertainty&quot;.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>589-590</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11673-017-9821-x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This response is a comment on the case of Jordan presented by Mason (2017). A key perspective we can take from this case is a consideration of: consumer motivations for testing, whether they have enough information and time to make a decision, and if the test they seek is entirely appropriate for them at their current stage of life.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
